 ## 7. Negative control (roundNC)
 
-The pre-registered negative-control round ran the same task on FBX, glTF and USDZ files with the same crate mesh and texture (3 trials per arm, 2026-10-11). On the frozen criteria werk passed 3 of 3 and the controls 0 of 9. That gap rests on rule R5 about "the primary mesh". The value comparisons used Windows 11 and Python 3.13.7 with UTF-8 mode. With a value-exact single sub-mesh accepted, glTF and FBX also pass 3 of 3 and USDZ 1 of 3. The robust differences are verifiability (werk 1.0 cryptographic, USDZ CRC-32 only, FBX and glTF none) and the file declaring its primary mesh. Isolation: 0 violations. Details and all artifacts are in the roundNC pull request (`gauntlet/roundNC/RESULTS-NC.md`).
+The pre-registered negative-control round ran the same task on FBX, glTF and USDZ files built from the CC0 crate (3 trials per arm, 2026-10-11). The assets are not matched: the control files carry the full crate (about 4 700 vertices), the werk arm used the 272-vertex crate in `mini-v1`, and the second payload is a texture in the controls and a sound in werk. So the round is exploratory. On the frozen criteria werk passed 3 of 3 and the controls 0 of 9. That gap rests on rule R5 about "the primary mesh". The value comparisons used Windows 11 and Python 3.13.7 with UTF-8 mode. With a value-exact single sub-mesh accepted, glTF and FBX also pass 3 of 3 and USDZ 1 of 3. The robust differences are verifiability (werk 1.0 cryptographic, USDZ CRC-32 only, FBX and glTF none) and the file declaring its primary mesh. Isolation: 0 violations. Details and all artifacts are in the roundNC pull request (`gauntlet/roundNC/RESULTS-NC.md`).
 
